                                "example_id": "28b9226c-754e-4b4f-b917-b605ce5cd403",
                                "sense_id": "d60cafa2-2934-31d9-8620-79ade94624a1",
                                "text": "I asked Thady a minute later what nests he knew of. \"Galore,\" he answered, grinning. And then proceeded to enumerate them : \" A lintie (a linnet), a green grosbeak (greenfinch), a Harry redcap (goldfinch), a yellow yeorling by the roadside, a scobby (chaffinch), a lavrock (skylark), a cushie-doo (a wood pigeon), a cutty wren (common wren), a nanny washtail (pied wagtail) in the rocks, and two tom-titers of sorts."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "03a529e4-74df-4e7d-b8db-1a516b1b0924",
                                "sense_id": "d60cafa2-2934-31d9-8620-79ade94624a1",
                                "text": "The brock, the toad, and the yellow yeorling Get a drap o' the de'il's bluid ilka May morning."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f7ec2a78-9165-4118-8e4f-e3dd9377e6ed",
                                "sense_id": "d60cafa2-2934-31d9-8620-79ade94624a1",
                                "text": "Then they listened to a yeorling and Will taught the child its song, \"A little bit of bread and no che-e-ese."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
